","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"Shri Kali Temple is a Hindu temple located in the undefined Little India in downtown Yangon, Burma. It was built by Tamil migrants in 1871, whilst Burma Province was part of British India. The temple is noted for its colorful architecture, especially its roof, which contains images and stone carvings of many Hindu gods.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Shri Kali Temple, Burma","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9b/Hindutempleyangon.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9b/Hindutempleyangon.jpg","w":1200,"h":1600,"author":"Xianzi Tan","license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.5","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hindutempleyangon.jpg"}},{"id":"yangon_kandawgyi_lake","areaId":"yangon","name":"Kandawgyi Lake","category":"park","tags":["nature","photo"],"location":{"lat":16.79549,"lng":96.16656},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"yangon_kandawgyi_lake","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":2,"commonsNearby":0,"wikiPageviews":274,"wikidataSitelinks":8,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-20"},"hashtags":["kandawgyilake","yangon"],"bestLight":"golden","summary":"Kandawgyi Lake is one of two major lakes in Yangon, Myanmar. Located east of the Shwedagon Pagoda, the lake is artificial; water from Inya Lake is channeled through a series of pipes to Kandawgyi Lake. It was created to provide a clean water supply to the city during the British colonial administration.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Kandawgyi Lake","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Kandawgyi_Lake%2C_Yangon.jpg/1280px-Kandawgyi_Lake%2C_Yangon.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/comm